From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:29:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: undo the depth layout when the CPU reads
 depth

Depth reaches memory through the color path: within each 80-pixel EDRAM
tile the 40-pixel halves are swapped, and each word is Mesa's Z24S8
byte-swapped and rotated by 8. Undo both when the CPU reads a
depth/stencil resource. Exact when the width is a multiple of 80; in a
partial last tile the swapped half lies past the row and keeps its old
contents (extending the resolve hung the GPU at some sizes; open).
CPU writes are left alone: depth textures the CPU uploads are sampled,
and the texture unit reads them in Mesa's layout.

